# Graphics drivers: the installer's « Pilote graphique » option and Settings > Graphics drivers
# (shell/main/lib/gpu-drivers.js, shell/main/ipc/installer.js, shell/main/ipc/drivers.js,
# /usr/lib/aurora/helpers/aurora-install, aurora-admin drivers-install / drivers-remove).
# The NVIDIA drivers themselves are NOT in the image: they are downloaded from the Ubuntu archive
# (restricted) when they are installed, with the prebuilt kernel modules signed by Canonical
# (linux-modules-nvidia-NNN-<flavour>), so Secure Boot keeps working without enrolling a key.
# `ubuntu-drivers devices` / `ubuntu-drivers install nvidia:NNN[-open]` (+ gpu-manager for hybrid laptops).
ubuntu-drivers-common
# Secure Boot state only (`mokutil --sb-state`). lspci (pciutils) is in base.list.
mokutil
